  by: agent  # 0a37
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0a37
  clock: 4  # 0a37
  nonce: 0a37  # 0a37
  message: "MEASURED 2026-08-06. Full write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/INV-linub-CHAIN-MEASUREMENT.md. Instrument meas/chain_probe.py, fixtures meas/fixtures/. HEADLINE: not one of the nine at-risk languages legitimately matches a method-kind sink. The only match in the table is go TWOSTEP, and it is a bare-name FALSE POSITIVE (is_resolved=True on an external-shaped dst routes into the ungated hits[0] fallback). VALIDATION: emission agrees with WI-nasuf published cells on all six previously-measured languages, which is what licenses the new cells. MATCHING differs on four of them because the published cell overstates what was measured (see the correction filed on WI-nasuf). THE CLASS IS TWO CHANNELS NOT ONE: false negatives (L2 emission gaps AND a universal L3 receiver-typing gap that no filed item covered) and false positives (is_resolved bypass; INV-fokik corrupted module hint). CRITICAL: fixing L2 alone moves NOTHING - java, scala, swift, python-twostep, rust and objc all emit today and all fail at L4 because gate_named_entry refuses an untyped method call unconditionally. MECHANISMS read in code: THREE shapes, not nine. kotlin = resolver-lookup gate with no unresolved fallback; python + javascript = too-narrow syntactic receiver whitelist; java = emission works but the module segment carries the VARIABLE NAME while the receiver TYPE it already computes (var_types) is routed only to meta[receiver_type_hint] for Tier-2 linkers. That last one is the cheapest fix available. STILL VOID: rust and objc cells (controls broken); java and scala have NO possible sink-based positive control because 100% of their catalogued entries are gated on receiver typing."  # 0a37
- op: discuss  # f21c
  at: '2026-08-06T06:55:33Z'  # f21c
  by: agent  # f21c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f21c
  clock: 5  # f21c
  nonce: f21c  # f21c
  message: "FIRST FIX LANDED: PR #227 (dev 64d8db5da2), the java receiver-typing half. Java typed-local now emits java:java.io.File:0-0:createNewFile:unresolved and REACHES java.io.File.createNewFile through production _match_propagation_entry - the first legitimate method-kind sink match in the nine-language table (go was a bare-name FP, INV-fazim). Chosen first because the type was already computed in var_types and merely routed to meta[receiver_type_hint] for Tier-2 linkers, so it was the cheapest available test of the L3 thesis. THE THESIS HELD. DIRECTION MEASURED ON BOTH SIGNS, and the fix opened a channel that had to be closed inside the same PR: naming the type also SHORTENS the callee from w.doFinal to doFinal, and _register_sanitizer_callers matches on the SHORT NAME while never reading the module hint - so com.example.Widget.doFinal bound the catalogued javax.crypto.Cipher.doFinal. That phantom barrier registered for real, it was not hypothetical. A phantom barrier earns sanitized and DROPS the flow (#214), so the recall win would have been paid for in deleted findings. Guard: make_unresolved_edge grew an additive call_construct kwarg and the branch declares method, which both taint gates honour; costs nothing on the sink side because _lookup_named_entry returns from its module-filter branch before gate_named_entry runs. Post-guard barriers are ZERO in both directions - phantom AND earned - because the sanitizer path has no module filtering to tell them apart. Deliberate trade per that function own ruling. STILL OPEN ON THIS CLASS: java CHAINED (receiver-shape, not typing); java fully-qualified declarations (inferred type is java.io.File while imports is keyed by simple name - this is why java CONTROL is still BROKEN in the probe); kotlin (needs the unresolved fallback it lacks entirely); python + javascript (need the syntactic receiver whitelist widened); rust + objc cells still VOID on broken controls."  # f21c
- op: discuss  # 6185
  at: '2026-08-06T17:21:05Z'  # 6185
  by: agent  # 6185
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6185
  clock: 6  # 6185
  nonce: '6185'  # 6185
  message: "THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT UNDER-SCOPES ITS OWN CONSEQUENCE. Measured 2026-08-06,\nscripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py, positive control passed (pretix: 443,296\nedges offered to _is_taint_call_edge, 191,264 accepted, 69 summary entries,\n31,913 callees_at entries -- no stage empty).\n\nThe filed chain is L1 catalogue -> L2 emission -> L3 receiver evidence -> L4 the\nF3 gate, and the statement says the evidence must be enough \"for\n_match_propagation_entry to return that catalogue entry\". That names ONE\nconsumer of L3. There is a SECOND, and it is what manufactures the largest\nblocker family on INV-busis:\n\n    _qualified_callee -> _catalogue_key_for_edge -> callees_at\n        -> _use_site_terminates  (inside the ADR-0017 section 3a walk)\n\n_module_from_symbol_path returns \"\" for the \"external\" placeholder BY\nDOCUMENTED DESIGN, so _qualified_callee yields no key, so the edge never\nreaches callees_at, so _use_site_terminates cannot decide, so the walk records\nan ESCAPE. Same missing module slot, different downstream victim: not a\ncatalogue MATCH failure but a section 4 SUMMARY LOOKUP failure.\n\nEVIDENCE. On pretix, 13 of 17 call-node escape sites (76.5%) carry a dst of the\nform python:external:0-0:NAME:external_symbol -- the literal placeholder --\nfor save, confirm, delete, get, refresh_from_db, create_external_refund,\nlog_action, append, create. ZERO of them lack an edge. The edges are emitted\nand then discarded for want of a receiver type.\n\nTwo sub-causes must not be folded, and the instrument now splits them:\n  3a  UNRESOLVED edge with the external placeholder  -> this class, a defect\n  3b  RESOLVED first-party callee refused by the WI-zumud provenance gate\n      -> CORRECT behaviour, not a gap (1 of 17 on pretix, PaypalMethod.init_api)\n\nPYTHON HAS THE TYPE AND IS NOT USING IT, which is exactly where java was before\nPR #227 (\"the type was already in var_types, routed only to meta\"). py.py\ncarries var_types and external_var_types; PR #231's emit site hardcodes the\nplaceholder and its own comment says so -- \"the receiver's type is genuinely\nunknown here\". At that branch it is; the question this class should answer is\nwhether the tracked type is reachable there, as java's was.\n\nBUT THE DIRECTION WARNING IS THE OPPOSITE OF THE OBVIOUS ONE, AND IT IS NOT\nLIVE TODAY. Giving these calls a qualified key lets _use_site_terminates return\nTrue more often, which produces MORE False verdicts, which since PR #214 earns\nsanitized and DROPS flows -- suppressive. Measured counterweight: of the three\npretix sites that did get a key, two hit \"no summary\" and one hit \"propagates\";\nnone closed. And measured bound: there are ZERO barrier-arm walks on any of the\nfour repos that produce walks at all (hypergumbo 36, pretix 35, prometheus 7,\nalertmanager 3 -- every invocation on the 3a arm, where False and None\ncollapse), so nothing here can move a finding in either direction today.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THIS CLASS: the \"measure through L4, on findings, not through\nL2 on edges\" rule still holds and is now doubly justified -- L4 is not the only\ngate downstream of L3, and BOTH downstream consumers are currently inert for\nfindings. Any fix under this class should state which consumer it targets."  # 6185
