- op: discuss  # 3c97
  at: '2026-08-06T18:29:33Z'  # 3c97
  by: agent  # 3c97
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3c97
  clock: 8  # 3c97
  nonce: 3c97  # 3c97
  message: "CORRECTION AND ESCALATION, same day. My note above said this item's\nstatement under-scopes its consequence by naming one downstream consumer\nwhen there are two. There are THREE.\n\nWHAT I CLAIMED, HOURS EARLIER TODAY: zero barrier-arm walks BECAUSE the\nshipped sanitizer vocabulary is crypto-only -- and therefore \"a sanitizer\ncatalogue ARMS the removal hazard; catalogue growth creates the danger, so\ngates land before catalogue growth.\"\n\nWHY IT WAS NOT ESTABLISHED: I never positive-controlled the zero. A null\nbelieved without demonstrating the instrument can produce a known positive is\nthe exact rule this repo has written down, and I violated it the same day I\nedited it into LIVE.md. It is also the shape of this area's own invalidated\n0.00% confident-negative figure: a tautology of the configuration.\n\nTWO PURPOSE-BUILT FIXTURES, BOTH ZERO WALKS:\n  v1  f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain);\n      pathlib.Path(...).write_text(cipher)\n      -> the crypto calls emit python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol.\n         The receiver type is never inferred, so the SOURCE cannot match\n         cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt and the SANITIZER cannot match\n         Fernet.encrypt. No flow exists for a barrier to guard.\n  v2  the same shape written MODULE-QUALIFIED, removing receiver typing as a\n      variable -> source and sanitizer now resolve\n      (python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol), but the\n      SINK emits NO call edge at all: pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x) is an\n      attribute chain rooted at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT. Still zero walks.\n\nSO THE BARRIER ARM IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE SAME ROOT CAUSE AS THE REST OF THIS\nAREA. Every sanitizer in the shipped catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD --\nFernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal -- and\ninstance-method receiver typing is precisely what is broken (INV-linub). That\nis a THIRD symptom family from one root cause, alongside io-boundary catalogue\nreach and the section 4 summary lookup inside the walk.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: the observation (0 barrier walks across 4 repos and 2 fixtures)\nand the practical verdict (an escape reclassification cannot move a finding\ntoday). WHAT DOES NOT: the mechanism, and every sequencing conclusion built on\nit. Catalogue growth CANNOT arm the hazard while receiver typing is broken.\nRECEIVER TYPING IS WHAT ARMS IT.\n\nSTILL OPEN, stated rather than papered over: I could not construct a barrier\nwalk in ANY configuration, so I cannot distinguish \"reachable, and nothing in\nthe corpus hits it\" from \"effectively dead on the DDG path\". There is also NO\nend-to-end test driving the barrier arm through propagate_taint_ddg -- the one\n'sanitized' test uses propagate_taint_structural. A positive control is a\nprerequisite for any future claim about this arm, mine included.\n\nTHE THIRD CONSUMER: the ADR-0017 SANITIZER BARRIER ARM. Every sanitizer\nin the shipped catalogue is an instance method, so registering one\nrequires exactly the receiver evidence this class is about. With it\nmissing, sanitizer_lines stays empty, barrier_sites is empty, and the\nguarded walk never runs. So this class gates:\n  L4 io-boundary catalogue match  (filed)\n  section 4 summary lookup in the 3a walk  (added earlier today)\n  the sanitizer barrier arm entirely  (this note)\n\nA SLOT OBSERVATION FROM FIXTURE v2, NOT YET RUN DOWN: when the call IS\nmodule-qualified the analyzer emits module=cryptography.fernet.Fernet,\nname=decrypt, while the catalogue declares module=cryptography.fernet,\nname=Fernet.decrypt. The class name sits in a DIFFERENT SLOT on each\nside. Whether _match_propagation_entry normalises that is unverified --\nfixture v2 died on its sink before the question could be answered. It is\nrecorded because it is the INV-fokik shape (slot assumptions) wearing\ndifferent clothes, and a fix here that assumes the slots line up would\nbe measured as working while matching nothing.\n\nPRIORITY CONSEQUENCE: this class is now upstream of the entire refutation\nquestion, not just of catalogue reach. Every remaining measurement in the\ntaint area is confounded until it lands."  # 3c97
- op: discuss  # 4690
  at: '2026-08-06T22:04:43Z'  # 4690
  by: agent  # 4690
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4690
  clock: 9  # 4690
  nonce: '4690'  # 4690
  message: "CONSUMER COUNT CORRECTED, 2026-08-06: TWO, not three. The third consumer\nclaimed on this thread yesterday -- \"the sanitizer barrier arm entirely\" --\nwas WRONG, and it was the second wrong mechanism proposed for the barrier\narm's zero (the first was a thin crypto-only catalogue). Both were filed\nwithout a positive control; both are retracted.\n\nESTABLISHED, with the control that was missing: the arm was blocked by\nINV-funit -- _register_sanitizer_callers read the NAME slot for receiver\nevidence that production puts in the MODULE slot, so its permit branch was\nunreachable for every method-shaped sanitizer. A probe with receiver typing\nWORKING (parameter annotation, taint_refine pinned\npython:cryptography.fernet.Fernet into the module slot, source matched, walk\nadjudicated `precise`) STILL produced zero barrier walks, because the\nsanitizer was refused independently. Receiver typing is NECESSARY for the\nunannotated case and NOT SUFFICIENT for any case. Fixed in dev 8b1a20cc1b;\nthe arm now fires on idiomatic code.\n\nTHE TWO SURVIVING CONSUMERS:\n  (1) io-boundary catalogue match -- gate_named_entry returns None for an\n      untyped `method` call. This is the one the item's statement names.\n  (2) the section 4 summary lookup inside the section 3a walk --\n      _qualified_callee -> _catalogue_key_for_edge -> callees_at, since\n      _module_from_symbol_path returns \"\" for the `external` placeholder BY\n      DOCUMENTED DESIGN. This manufactures INV-busis's largest escape family\n      and is the SURVIVING reason this item ranks ahead of INV-mumov.\n\nThe promotion argument therefore stands, on (2) alone rather than on three\nlegs. Recording the weakening explicitly so the ordering is re-derivable\nrather than inherited.\n\nREACH LIMIT worth carrying into WI-nasuf/WI-zilag: the module slot reaches\ntaint only for python (taint_refine's annotation pinning, gated\nlang == \"python\" at cli.py) and java (PR #227's analyzer emit). Go, rust and\ntypescript cannot present one at all today."  # 4690
- op: discuss  # e018
  at: '2026-08-08T21:03:19Z'  # e018
  by: agent  # e018
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e018
  clock: 10  # e018
  nonce: e018  # e018
  message: "SPLIT AND RESCOPE. The statement is over-quantified on three axes and conflates\ntwo different failures.\n\nMEASURED (7 Py repos, 49,811 unique catalogue-name call sites):\n  catalogue reach 8,009 = 16.08%  (23.0% excluding sqlalchemy)\n  usable receiver evidence 10,184 = 20.45%\n  receiver-typing delta from #244/#246/#247: +193 sites, replicated EXACTLY on\n  7/7 repos; 0 sites reached before and stopped reaching after.\n  Conditional on evidence being present, the L4 gate admits 78.6% (87.0% on\n  non-ambiguous method names) -- so THE WALL IS L3 (receiver evidence), NOT L4.\n\nTHREE OVER-QUANTIFICATIONS:\n 1. \"for every language\" -- only Python was measured. Demote to a per-language\n    clause.\n 2. \"regardless of the receiver syntax used\" -- it IS true today for a definable\n    subset: receiver is an imported module, an annotated parameter, or a\n    TYPE_PRESERVING_MEMBERS derivation thereof. Enumerate the in-scope syntaxes\n    rather than quantifying over all of them.\n 3. Emission and receiver evidence are one clause and are different failures.\n    Split: clause A (an edge exists at all -- INV-mumov's territory) vs clause B\n    (the edge carries receiver evidence).\n\nDENOMINATOR CORRECTION: 32.9% of the measured population (sqlalchemy, 16,725\nsites) has ZERO catalogue entries -- unreachable at L1, an axis this item\nexplicitly defers. Fix or exclude that before sizing anything here; it inflates\nthe blocker ~2.9x.\n\nLARGEST OPEN INSTANCE: untyped bare-Name receiver, 7,282 of 16,818 non-reaching\nsites (43.3%); its top sub-family is receiver-assigned-from-a-call-result\n(2,693, 37.0%).\n\nDO NOT PRIORITISE `.parent` -- 16 sites, 0.7% of chain-on-Name misses.\n\nNOT MEASURED: taint's own _match_propagation_entry (the io-boundary consumer was\nmeasured as a proxy); any non-Python language; findings-level effect of the +193."  # e018
- op: discuss  # 7d05
  at: '2026-08-09T01:53:25Z'  # 7d05
  by: agent  # 7d05
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7d05
  clock: 11  # 7d05
  nonce: 7d05  # 7d05
  message: "CORRECTION to the 2026-08-08 note on this thread, which is replicated verbatim on\nINV-linub, INV-mumov and WI-zilag. Adjudicated by four independent measurement lenses\nplus three adversarial refuters each; the numbers below are only those that survived\nrefutation, and the refuted ones are named at the bottom so they are not re-cited.\n\n1. \"32.9% of the measured population (sqlalchemy, 16,725 sites)\" IS A COHORT ARTIFACT,\n   NOT A CATALOGUE GAP. The sqlalchemy REPO was one of the 7 repos measured (pretix,\n   sqlalchemy, mitmproxy, poetry, pyright, meson, kserve). All 16,994 rows in the\n   sqlalchemy artifact carry file paths under ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/sqlalchemy/,\n   and the instrument's own REPOS constant names it. It was never call sites INTO\n   sqlalchemy-as-a-dependency. Confirmed independently by three lenses; that 7-repo\n   cohort contains ZERO sqlalchemy consumers, so it could not have tested the other\n   reading even in principle.\n\n2. \"it inflates the blocker ~2.9x\" IS WRONG FOR REACH. The true factor is 1.47x\n   (50,772 population) / 1.48x (49,811). The genuine 2.9x belongs to a DIFFERENT\n   family -- CALL_RESULT_ROOT no-edge, 8,962 total of which sqlalchemy is 5,826 =\n   2.86x, which is INV-mumov's territory. The factor was computed on one family and\n   applied to another.\n\n3. \"ZERO catalogue entries -- unreachable at L1\" IS DIAGNOSTICALLY WRONG. sqlalchemy\n   has 88-93 REACHING sites (builtins.open 20, os.path.exists 11, os.remove 11). Its\n   denominator is dominated by short-name COLLISIONS with catalogue entries -- execute\n   3,228, all 1,721, order_by 1,362, filter, get, commit -- whose only catalogue homes\n   are django.db.models / sqlite3. Those sites MUST NOT reach. 52.7% of them are in\n   ambiguous_names. The remedy for a collision is not a catalogue entry.\n\n4. TWO POPULATIONS, ONE PROBE -- name one and stay in it. 50,772 (plain\n   (file,line,name) dedup) and 49,811 (agg2.py's uniq()) come from the same row set\n   under two aggregation rules, reproduced 7/7 per repo in both directions. PREFER\n   50,772 AND SAY SO: uniq() DELETES BOTH MEMBERS of a colliding site, dropping 961\n   distinct sites that are reach-depleted (8.1% vs 16.06%), so 49,811 is the truncated\n   population and mildly INFLATES every reach rate.\n\n5. NEW, AND IT UNDERCUTS THE L4 FIGURES ON THIS THREAD: django.db.models-stamped sites\n   reach at 4,623/4,623 = 100.00% BY CONSTRUCTION -- py.py:527 hard-codes the module\n   string, python.yaml holds the same 29 names, and _module_matches on identical\n   strings is unconditionally True. That family is 57.3% of the reach numerator. Strip\n   it and L4-admit-given-evidence falls 78.69% -> 61.22%. The 87.0% D3 figure is\n   pretix at 99.34% against 54.84% for the other six repos. Do not quote 78.6%/87.0%\n   as a general result.\n\n6. INV-mumov's \"15.2%\" reproduces from NO candidate denominator any lens tried. Treat\n   it as unsourced.\n\nREFUTED 3/3, DO NOT RE-CITE: a \"cross-instrument splice\" between two different probes\n(there is one probe, two aggregation rules); and the whole \"no long tail / 2.53%\nthird-party / bounded curation\" family -- its census admits a site only if the method\nname is ALREADY in python.yaml, which excludes by construction every name curation\nwould add, and adding two out-of-cohort repos moved distinct third-party packages\n52 -> 88 with no saturation.\n\nARTIFACT INTEGRITY: the run that produced the 32.9%/23.0% anchor (inv8/denom-inference)\ncarries an ENOSPC traceback in its own log. The per-repo rows are self-consistent and\nreproduce, but that artifact was written under the WI-kovoj disk trap.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE WORK: there is no L1 catalogue fix to make here. The real\nuser-facing defect found while adjudicating this paragraph is filed separately as\nINV-fibis (verify-claims returns `confirmed` for a boundary reachable through modules\nthe catalogue cannot adjudicate -- reproduced on poetry and full-stack-fastapi-template\nwith a positive control firing in the same run)."  # 7d05
