- op: discuss  # 5798
  at: '2026-08-28T03:29:49Z'  # 5798
  by: agent  # 5798
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5798
  clock: 41  # 5798
  nonce: '5798'  # 5798
  message: "RUST L3 HALF-CLOSED AND MEASURED. PR #595 (dev 51ef19395e).\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. The earlier L3 fix recovered an external receiver's module path\nthrough use_aliases, which fires only when the type was imported BY NAME. When\nthe source WRITES the path -- `fn dump(f: &mut std::fs::File)`, or\n`let start = std::time::Instant::now()` with no `use` --\n_normalize_rust_type_to_bare_name reduces it to `File` / `Instant` (\"strip\nmodule paths\", per its own docstring, which is correct for the first-party\nsymbol lookups it feeds) and the bare name is then absent from use_aliases. A\nsecond file-scoped map now carries the written path beside the bare one,\nconsulted only on the unresolved-external branch. It cannot invent one: a value\nis returned only when the text contains `::` AND the path's terminal segment\nequals the bare name the normalizer produced, which binds the two readings of\none type. `std::io::Result<std::fs::File>` normalizes to `File` while the text\nstarts with `Result`, so it yields nothing rather than stamping the wrong\nmodule and turning a correct L4 refusal into a confident mismatch.\n\nA/B, 11 rust repos of the frame_08252026 screen, per-arm XDG_CACHE_HOME, arms\nstrictly sequential, each arm proven live before it ran:\n\n  catalogued trait-method sites matched   41/1202 -> 98/1206   (3.4% -> 8.1%)\n  rust call sites given an I/O boundary   303 -> 360           (+18.8%)\n     host_info_read                       68 -> 116\n     fs_read                              50 -> 59\n  CONTROLS unchanged: env_read 29, env_write 19, fs_write 63, ipc_recv 7,\n     logging 15, subprocess 52  (6 of 8 boundaries)\n\nIT MOVES NO TAINT FLOW: 2 -> 2, and the reason is structural. 48 of the 57 new\nmatches are Instant::elapsed, a host_info_read -- which IS in\nAUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP and can seed, but no clock read reaches a write-side sink\nin this cohort. The other 9 are fs_read rows (exists, canonicalize, is_dir,\nmetadata), which are neither source nor sink BY DESIGN, since fs_read is\ndeliberately excluded from the source map. So this is an io-boundaries\nimprovement and it is recorded as one, not as a taint improvement. It is\nexactly the capability-is-not-recall shape this item warned about, arriving\nfrom the L3 side instead of the L2 side.\n\nMY EARLIER DENOMINATOR WAS WRONG AND IS WITHDRAWN. A first cut reported \"113 of\n7035 external method sites, 1.6%\". That denominator is EVERY external method\ncall, dominated by first-party receivers (Tensor.matmul, VarBuilder.pp) that\nmust never match a catalogue row. This item's denominator is the AVAILABLE\ncatalogued trait-method call site, and on it the figure is 8.1%.\n\nDENOMINATOR CAVEAT ON THIS ITEM'S OWN FILED CELL. The cell reads \"0 method-kind\nmatches / 78 available\". On the current tree the available count is 1202-1206,\nnot 78, because four commits grew the rust catalogue after that cell was\nwritten (sources 23 -> 63, sinks 30 -> 84). The 0 -> 41 -> 98 progression is\nreal; the 78 is not comparable to the 1206.\n\nWHAT IS STILL OPEN FOR RUST, filed rather than folded in: WI-dizag\n(struct-field receiver) and WI-papar (chained receiver + the try-expression\n`?` form). write_all matched 5 and MISSED 125; `lock` misses 440. Both live on\nthe SINK side -- fs_write is an auto-derived sink -- so unlike this fix they can\nmove a verdict. The rust row of this item's table should now read L3 PARTIAL,\nnot L3 FAILS."  # 5798
