- op: discuss  # 477c
  at: '2026-09-03T00:26:35Z'  # 477c
  by: agent  # 477c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 477c
  clock: 45  # 477c
  nonce: 477c  # 477c
  message: "THE BAND NO LONGER TRIPS, ON EITHER ESTIMATOR. Reporting only -- the priority\nchange is the owner's.\n\nMeasurement 0012 (docs/measurements/0012-taint-precision-after-escape-closure.md),\nrun under 0006's ratified frame on the same 16 repositories at dev f247b52587:\n\n  useful precision, pooled                30.9%  (29/94)\n  useful precision, unweighted repo mean  28.0%\n  correctness precision, pooled           34.0%  (32/94)\n  0006, for comparison                    24.1%  (27/112)\n\nThe standing gate is \"<=25% useful => recall work stays stopped\". 30.9% and\n28.0% both clear it.\n\nTHE OBJECTION THIS MEASUREMENT WAS BUILT TO ANSWER, and its answer. n=94 mixes\n68 situations carrying 0006's own labels with 26 judged fresh. The carry\ninvites a survivorship reading: the 68 are 0006's sample filtered by SURVIVAL,\nso fixes that removed only bad findings would lift their rate without the tool\nimproving. The 26 fresh exist to close that hole and are drawn from a\npopulation that has changed by ~600 situations.\n\n  68 carried   correctness 30.9%   useful 30.9%\n  26 fresh     correctness 42.3%   useful 30.8%\n\nThe two strata agree to a tenth of a point on the figure the band reads. That\nis evidence AGAINST the survivorship objection, not proof of its absence: one\ndraw of 26 has a wide interval.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH, stated because the gate is being reported as\nclear. It is not independent of 0006 -- 68 of 94 labels ARE 0006's. No A/B was\nrun, so no fix is attributed. Precision is not recall: nothing in 0012 measures\nthe defect THIS item describes, and the entire remaining gap between\ncorrectness (34.0%) and useful (30.9%) is INV-nular, not this.\n\nThe deadlock LIVE rule 18 names is unchanged in structure -- the band stops\nrecall, and receiver typing is classed as recall -- but the band's own\ncondition is now the one that has moved."  # 477c
